  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "web-note",
      "x": 1580,
      "y": 1220,
      "w": 320,
      "page": "desktop",
      "text": "Web, 1280 wide — the Stitch look on the app's web layout.\n\nInter, emerald header with pill nav, white 16px cards on slate. Content is a 996px column.\n\nFive tabs now: Ward Map sits between Today and Forecast. Its areas are grey because the app has no CPCB station key yet — it draws no colour rather than inventing readings.\n\nAnalytics covers 2015–2025; the 2015–2019 dots are hollow because those years come from a second source that reads about 10 AQI higher.\n\nToday, Forecast and AI Chat are live: tap a day, a month or a year, switch language. The moon icon flips dark mode."
    },
    {
      "id": "phone-note",
      "x": 2450,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 300,
      "page": "phone",
      "text": "The same pages under 860px, where the app collapses to one column.\n\nNot a separate product — the identical markup reflowed. Kept here so the narrow breakpoint has a reference too."
    },
    {
      "id": "editorial-note",
      "x": 1380,
      "y": 1080,
      "w": 320,
      "page": "editorial",
      "text": "Retired. The \"editorial calm\" direction the app used before it moved to the Stitch look on 14 September 2026.\n\nKept for reference only — the app no longer matches these boards."
    }
